  "generated_text": "1. **Simplify the expression**:\n   \\[\n   5^5 - 5^3 = 5^3(5^2 - 1) = 5^3(25 - 1) = 5^3 \\cdot 24\n   \\]\n\n2. **Factorize 24**:\n   \\[\n   24 = 2^3 \\cdot 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Combine the factors**:\n   \\[\n   5^3 \\cdot 24 = 5^3 \\cdot 2^3 \\cdot 3\n   \\]\n\n4. **Identify distinct prime factors**:\n   The distinct prime factors are 2, 3, and 5.\n\n5. **Sum the distinct prime factors**:\n   \\[\n   2 + 3 + 5 = 10\n   \\]\n\nConclusion:\nThe sum of the distinct prime factors of $5^5 - 5^3$ is $\\boxed{10}$.",
  "grade": {
